      {
        "type": "Module",
        "name": "power_supervisor",
        "description": "TPS3703 monitors the regulated 3.3V rail and generates a POWER_GOOD status indication through its RESET output. This module is powered from the same VCC_3V3 rail that it supervises, and its SENSE input must observe that rail directly so the monitored threshold tracks the delivered 3.3V output. CT and MR require downstream configuration/support networks because their behavior is part-dependent and no assumptions are made here; the intended topology is a standard voltage-monitoring function with a single status output. If RESET is open-drain in the selected implementation, downstream wiring must assign pull-up ownership on the receiving domain; if push-pull, route directly as a logic status signal.",
        "id": "power_supervisor"
      },
      {
        "type": "Component",
        "refdes": "U2",
